Z||000000||frontal lobe||12-28-2001||02:28 AM||||My wife wanted a radio/stereo just for use in the kitchen.  $400 plus for a Bose wave cd/radio, which I understand is decent to good for a small room like that, but I felt was a rip.<P>So I got a JVC fs-sd990 mini-system for her for less than 1/2 that, hid it in a cabinet shelf for her with the speakers on top of the cabinets out of view, and we both are happy.  The system could use better bass, though, and there is a subwoofer out so here is my question:  can anyone give me some advice on getting a somewhat decent, smaller sized subwoofer for &lt; $100.  I don't need it to rattle the plates or anything.  It's just a kitchen.  I've seen a sony one for $100, and I can order a JVC 50 watt one for $100.  Just curious if anyone has any ideas.<P>Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000001||chester||12-28-2001||08:07 AM||||Best Buy has a couple of powered subs under $100.<P>Rob D. <BR> <P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
